const studyDefaults={
 EXP26007104:{title:'Cyclin D1/CypA NanoBRET tag-configuration study · 14 compounds · 24 hours',description:'Compare Cyclin D1 N- and C-terminal NanoLuc with CypA N- and C-terminal HaloTag across four configurations, with dose responses in technical duplicate and two independent biological replicates.',id:'EXP26007104',benchling:'',context:'14 full compound IDs × 4 configurations = 56 curves per biological replicate. Replicate 1: 25 Sep 2026; replicate 2: 30 Sep 2026. A = NLN/HTC; B = NLN/HTN; C = NLC/HTN; D = NLC/HTC. Source annotations match the supplied key. Latest GDS corrected values use ratio normalization. Replicate 1 plate assignments were corrected in the latest export: 01B = NLN/HTN; 01D = NLC/HTC. No sample or control wells are masked in either run. Independent ratio refits remain separate from reported GDS parameters. The supplied exports cover 24 hours only; no 2-hour results are included.'},
 EXP26007301:{title:'Screening 26 compounds with EC50 <3 µM against Cyclin D3, Cyclin E1, Cyclin K and CDK4',description:'24-hour experiment using GDS well-level and parameter exports to compare corrected dose responses, reported potency, raw plate measurements and technical replicate agreement.',id:'EXP26007301',benchling:'EXP26007301',context:'27 unique compound/batch identities in the supplied data: 26 library compounds plus RMC-0741051 reference on both plates. The source uses 28 labels because the plate-2 reference has a separate source label; both reference readings are the same batch -001. Tested against Cyclin D3, Cyclin E1, Cyclin K and CDK4 at 24 hours. Biological replicate 1: 9 Oct 2026; replicate 2: 15 Oct 2026. Both runs include corrected-well curves and matched GDS reports with Cmax, qAC50/EC50, qualifiers and QC flags. Each target uses two compound plates (01 and 02): A = Cyclin D3, B = Cyclin E1, C = Cyclin K, D = CDK4. Original export labels and any assignment corrections are retained in curve details and Methods.'},
 EXP26003438:{title:'Dose Response Follow-up of the 1CC and 1CN CypA TCI Library screening in Cyclin D1/CypA NanoBRET at RevMed -20260720',description:'Purpose: Dose response follow-up of CypA TCI Library hits identified in the Pharmaron primary screen. The pooled NanoBRET assay combines N- and C-terminal NanoLuc-tagged target protein with CypA_HTN and CypA_HTC, in 384-well plates with duplicate compound dose responses at Revolution Medicines.',id:'EXP26003438',benchling:'https://revmed.benchling.com/revmed/f/lib_gdrBEMwl-cell-biology-screening/etr_cjTdywkDil-dose-response-follow-up-of-the-1cc-and-1cn-cypa-tci-library-screening-in-cyclin-d1cypa-nanobret-at-revmed-20260720/edit',context:'306 library IDs plus positive reference RMC-0741051-001 across two biological replicates. Per your confirmation, paired A/B plates contain the same compounds at the same concentrations; A is compound without CypA inhibitor and B adds 25 µM CypA inhibitor. The replicate folders are 20260902 and 20260904 (instrument dates Sep 2 and Sep 3, respectively). Curves are reconstructed from raw acceptor/donor ratios and plate controls, with the supplied corrected B export used to verify replicate 1. The separate source parameter report labels 143 library compounds “increasing”; its fitted parameters are displayed separately because the export does not identify a specific replicate/plate assignment. DMSO = column 22; no-HaloTag = column 23.'}
};
